Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NoPM's web application (web/) and CLI (cli/) depend on open-source packages
distributed under their own licenses (MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0, BSD, and others).
Those packages are not modified and are not part of the NoPM copyright above;
their licenses travel with the packages themselves (typically inside
node_modules/<package>/LICENSE at install time, or in each package's own
repository). No NOTICE-level attribution is required for the MIT/ISC/BSD
majority of the dependency tree.

The following third-party components carry copyleft or non-trivial-permissive
licenses and are called out here for transparency (see
sprint-log/2026-09-07_open-source-release/reports/license-audit.md for the
full inventory and reasoning):

- axe-core (MPL-2.0) — accessibility-lint devDependency only; not distributed
  with the built application.
- lightningcss / lightningcss-win32-x64-msvc (MPL-2.0) — build-time CSS
  transform devDependency only (via Tailwind CSS v4 and Vite/vitest); not
  distributed with the built application.
- dompurify (MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0) — transitive runtime dependency of jspdf;
  used under the Apache-2.0 option of its dual license.
- jszip (MIT OR GPL-3.0-or-later) — transitive runtime dependency of
  pptxgenjs; used under the MIT option of its dual license.
- pako (MIT AND Zlib) — transitive dependency of jszip and jspdf; both
  component licenses are permissive.
- @img/sharp-win32-x64, @img/sharp-wasm32, and other @img/sharp-* platform
  packages (Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later[, AND MIT]) — optional prebuilt
  native/WASM image-processing binaries pulled in by Next.js's image
  optimizer (sharp); used as unmodified, dynamically-invoked prebuilt
  binaries, not statically linked into NoPM's own source.
- caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0) — browser-compatibility data table consumed at
  build time by Next.js/browserslist; a data license, not applied to NoPM's
  own code.
- minimatch@10.2.5 (BlueOak-1.0.0) — transitive devDependency (via
  typescript-eslint); permissive, attribution-only license.
- argparse (Python-2.0 license, not the GPL-incompatible "Python Software
  Foundation" license) — transitive devDependency of js-yaml/eslint; devtime
  only.
- rgbcolor (MIT, dual-offered with a custom "Feel free to use it" grant in
  FEEL-FREE.md) — transitive runtime dependency of jspdf/canvg; used under
  its MIT option.
- thirty-two — transitive runtime dependency of otplib; ships an MIT-text
  LICENSE.txt but omits the `license` field from package.json (classified
  "UNKNOWN" by automated scanners on metadata alone; the license file itself
  is plain MIT).

None of the above are modified from their published form. Full license texts
travel with each package in node_modules/ at install time (source: npm
registry) and are not reproduced in this NOTICE.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fonts
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Inter and JetBrains Mono are loaded via next/font/google (SIL Open Font
License 1.1) and self-hosted at build time; no font files are committed to
this repository. "SF Pro Text" / "SF Pro Display" / "SF Mono" appear only as
CSS font-family fallback names for macOS-native rendering — no Apple font
files are bundled or redistributed.

